Z||000014||Master_Sushi||10-23-2001||01:28 AM||||I've driven a 2000 V6 Stang auto. I have to say it was WAY easier to control a spin or fishtail then a Fiero. I was really pushing it to its limits and it was VERY predictable. When a Fiero goes out of control its almost always over, slam brakes on and enjoy the ride while hoping you don’t hit anything while skidding to a stop  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">.<P>You guys seem to begin insulting whenever you hear the word "mustang". I'm not defending them in any way. I’m just pointing out the obvious now.||||reg||13
Z||000015||Slammed Fiero||10-23-2001||01:43 AM||||The mustangs longer wheelbase is what makes it easy to control. Albeit has lower cornering ability.<P>The Fiero can easily bite you becuause of it's short wheelbase. Trailing throttle oversteer. It's a lot like driving a 911. Push it over the 10/10ths limit and it will bite you. But learn the limits and you have a killer!<P>I always find it fun to drive our mustang sideways , it's fairly easy to get it to kick out the tail. <P>Even more fun is a vette..you can drive it completley by the throttle. Torque Torque Torque!!<P>Just a different driving stlye is required. If you want to drive a car that can really bite you..Try an MR2...Higher cornering level than a Fiero in most instances..but a scary car at the limit.<P>JM ||||reg||1
