Z||000027||Return of Fiero||10-23-2001||01:44 PM||||hmm.. my 2 cents (i always have two cents, deep pockets i guess. lol) Back to my twins (you will hear refferances to them often) the upgraded one could "handle" better than just about anything i put it up against (flew down back roads on the tail of a porche corrara a few times) beat the pants off mustangs daily, and like the other person, looked for places to push the limits of the fiero. 60-70 in a twist 30 was common for me. the stock fiero was my winter driver, and it NEVER gave me a problem. i drove it every winter and NEVER lost control of either one. i have to agree with the nut behind the wheel coment. its 90% the driver, 4% the car, and 6% the condtions you are driving in. (weather, road conditions, etc.)<P>Myke||||reg||1
