Z||000033||Fiero5||10-23-2001||08:35 PM||||"Mr sushi your comments were quite intelligent, in another discussion they were flaming me about the fiero handling so much better."<P>That is because the Fiero DOES handle better than a Mustang. I have owned three Mustangs and 14 Fieros so far. The Mustangs are awesome cars, but they do not 'handle' better than a Fiero. LVMY88 had a great match against a stoopid Mustang owner. She was coming home in her then white w/red stripes 84 SE, and this local who owned a late model beefed up Mustang came up behind her reving his engine. They had seen each other for months, but always going in oposit directions. They were almost into Plainfield village, which is not a smart place to want to speed up. She knew that racing him that close to town would be pretty stoopid, so she just stayed at the speed limit minding her own business. He kept reving up and doing that stupid charge towards the rear of the other car crap  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_damon.gif"> . She knew what he would do at the top of the upcoming hill. Sure enough, as soon as they reached the top of the steep hill that goes down into Plainfield village (also happens to be passing there too) the Stang dude guns it and shows off how impressive he looks as he passes a car going the speed limit.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">  He must have been pretty impressed with looking at himself in his mirror or something, as he doesn't notice the NH state trooper that is just coming up from the bottom of the hill towards them. Ya gotta love timing  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>No sooner does the Stang blast past the trooper, the blue lights come on and you know what went thru the Stang drivers mind then LOL. The Stang driver immediatly pulls over knowing he's busted. Marian still doing the speed limit down the hill, just cruises by and smiles as she passes the poor slob getting a nice ticket.<BR>Nice car, stoopid owner. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif"> <BR> <BR>My black 81 Turbo Mustang was one awesome machine. Too bad Ford didn't make it out of enduraflex like the Fiero. I might still own it today  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><BR>But my fav Mustang was my 71 Mach 1. That was one incredible car. That huge 351 Cleveland beast ate as much gas as the competition it gobbled up.<P>I think we can all agree that usually it is the driver, not the car that does stoopid things.<P>Just my two pennies<P>Steve||||reg||12
Z||000034||Fierowrecker||10-23-2001||08:48 PM|||| <BLOCKQUOTE><font size="1" face="Verdana, Arial, Helvetica">quote:</font><HR>Originally posted by Slammed Fiero:<BR><B>The mustangs longer wheelbase is what makes it easy to control. Albeit has lower cornering ability.<P>The Fiero can easily bite you becuause of it's short wheelbase. Trailing throttle oversteer. It's a lot like driving a 911. Push it over the 10/10ths limit and it will bite you. But learn the limits and you have a killer!<P>I always find it fun to drive our mustang sideways , it's fairly easy to get it to kick out the tail. <P>Even more fun is a vette..you can drive it completley by the throttle. Torque Torque Torque!!<P>Just a different driving stlye is required. If you want to drive a car that can really bite you..Try an MR2...Higher cornering level than a Fiero in most instances..but a scary car at the limit.<P>JM </B><HR></BLOCKQUOTE><P>When I added my rear sway bar, much of the squirlyness went away...<BR>I take corners sideways in many types of driving conditions, dry, wet, sand, gravel, etc...<BR>Feels great to have a sport car that handles so nice! Now to boost the power a tad...||||reg||1
